[0.2,"o","$ "]
[0.3,"i","bt-intercom --help\r"]
[0.0,"o","bt-intercom --help\r\n"]
[0.25,"o","A Bluetooth headset intercom for Linux\r\n\r\nUsage: bt-intercom [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  scan        Scan for nearby Bluetooth devices\r\n  pair        Pair, trust, and connect a headset\r\n  remove      Remove a headset from the saved intercom network\r\n  status      Show Bluetooth headset audio status\r\n  run         Route configured headset microphones to one another\r\n  completions Generate shell completion definitions\r\n  tui         Open the terminal headset and talk-group control panel\r\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -v, --version  Print version\r\n      --verbose  Enable detailed diagnostics\r\n  -h, --help     Print help\r\n"]
[0.5,"o","$ "]
[0.4,"i","bt-intercom status AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02\r"]
[0.0,"o","bt-intercom status AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02\r\n"]
[0.3,"o","Alex (AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01): duplex ready (1 microphone ports, 1 speaker ports)\r\n  controller: hci0; HFP: true; A2DP: true\r\nJules (AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02): duplex ready (1 microphone ports, 1 speaker ports)\r\n  controller: hci1; HFP: true; A2DP: true\r\n"]
[0.5,"o","$ "]
[0.4,"i","bt-intercom run AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02 \\\r\n  --mode half-duplex --ptt AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01=auto \\\r\n  --ptt AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02=auto --transport sco-a2dp --dashboard\r"]
[0.0,"o","bt-intercom run AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02 \\\r\n  --mode half-duplex --ptt AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01=auto \\\r\n  --ptt AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02=auto --transport sco-a2dp --dashboard\r\n"]
[0.35,"o","INFO: Half-duplex: Hold play/pause to request the FIFO floor; release to cancel or relinquish. Double beep confirms a ready route.\r\n"]
[0.2,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2Jbt-intercom | half-duplex | muted | 0 owned active links\r\nHEADSET NAME             ADDRESS             CONNECTED  DUPLEX  TX/RX LINKS  SIGNAL\r\nAlex                     AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01  yes        yes      0/0          -58 dBm (strong)\r\nJules                    AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02  yes        yes      0/0          -66 dBm (good)\r\n\r\nLinks represent routing, not measured speech; RSSI is shown only if BlueZ reports it.\r\n"]
[3.0,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2Jbt-intercom | half-duplex | transmitting | 1 owned active links\r\nHEADSET NAME             ADDRESS             CONNECTED  DUPLEX  TX/RX LINKS  SIGNAL\r\nAlex                     AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01  yes        yes      1/0          -58 dBm (strong)\r\nJules                    AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02  yes        yes      0/1          -66 dBm (good)\r\n\r\nLinks represent routing, not measured speech; RSSI is shown only if BlueZ reports it.\r\n"]
[3.0,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2Jbt-intercom | half-duplex | muted | 0 owned active links\r\nHEADSET NAME             ADDRESS             CONNECTED  DUPLEX  TX/RX LINKS  SIGNAL\r\nAlex                     AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01  yes        yes      0/0          -58 dBm (strong)\r\nJules                    AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02  yes        yes      0/0          -66 dBm (good)\r\n\r\nLinks represent routing, not measured speech; RSSI is shown only if BlueZ reports it.\r\n"]
